Variables:

- $x_{sd} \geq 0$ (continuous), amount of cargo shipped from $s$ to $d$
- $t_{sd} \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$, number of trucks dispatched from $s$ to $d$

Model:

Minimize total transportation cost:
$$
\min \sum_{s \in S} \sum_{d \in D} c_{sd} \cdot x_{sd}
$$

Subject to:

1. Supply constraints (at each source):
$$
\sum_{d \in D} x_{sd} \leq S_s \qquad \forall s \in S
$$

2. Demand constraints (at each destination):
$$
\sum_{s \in S} x_{sd} = D_d \qquad \forall d \in D
$$

3. Truck loading constraints (each route):
$$
x_{sd} \leq 10 \cdot t_{sd} \qquad \forall s \in S,\, d \in D
$$

4. Integrality and nonnegativity:
$$
t_{sd} \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \qquad \forall s \in S,\, d \in D
$$
$$
x_{sd} \geq 0 \qquad \forall s \in S,\, d \in D
$$

Where:

- $S = \{\text{S1}, \ldots, \text{S10}\}$
- $D = \{\text{D1}, \ldots, \text{D20}\}$
- $S_s$ and $D_d$ as above
- $c_{sd}$ as above

